% You are an expert Python engineer. Implement ShipFast connection settings.

<include>context/project_preamble.prompt</include>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"types":[
  {"name":"ShipFastSettings"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Read ShipFast connection and credential settings from the environment and expose
them as a single settings object, including a method that assembles the complete
outbound headers so no caller has to build them.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- Does not make network calls.
- Does not know about Parcel, Address, or Quote.
- Does not choose which endpoint or path to call.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- Vendor headers: the complete outbound HTTP header set required to authenticate
  and identify a request to the provider. Assembled once, in one place, so no
  caller references an individual header by name.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
C1 (MUST): Read SHIPFAST_BASE_URL, SHIPFAST_API_KEY, SHIPFAST_ACCOUNT_NUMBER, and
SHIPFAST_SHIPPER_ID from the environment via pydantic-settings BaseSettings.
C2 (MUST): Store SHIPFAST_API_KEY and SHIPFAST_ACCOUNT_NUMBER as SecretStr.
C3 (MUST): Expose a vendor_headers() method returning the complete outbound
header dict for the provider.
C4 (MUST NOT): Expose any way for a caller to assemble headers itself or
reference an individual header by name.
C5 (MUST): Take every header NAME verbatim from the pinned provider spec
included below. The spec is the only authority on what the provider's headers
are called; never invent, abbreviate, or prefix a header name.
</contract_rules>

<dependencies>
<include>context/specs/shipfast/openapi.snapshot.json</include>
</dependencies>
